    "rating": 4.4,
    "reference": "ChIJf2c6Fhc3yUwR1n14niy30EY",
    "reviews": [
      {
        "author_name": "Sig & Connie Giron De Micco",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111580283661815104552/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocIlBy1Al6R29LuJUWB7dvzSRxxkt7lKw1aWAkNT7ytiuTsHZQ=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "a month ago",
        "text": "*UPDATE JAN 8TH: The owner commented on my review asking to complete the customer service form, which we had already done prior to this public response. Unfortunately, despite doing so, the issues remained unresolved, which is why this review was posted. (Photo attached). Not to mention the soundbar we ordered with the store credit that was forced on us to take rather than getting our money back (even though it was their mistake), Patrick told us that the soundbar would be here within a few days (this conversation was on Dec 30th), we heard nothing from them since this talk and so we called only to find out that it'll only be there in 3 weeks!! A few days and 3 weeks is not the same thing. False promises and so unprofessional*\n\nWhere do I start? We purchased a mattress, bed frame, and headboard here and we were very excited. While the mattress is comfortable, we were told the bed frame did not require a box spring.\n\nOn the first night, we heard cracking noises all night. The next morning, we saw that the legs were slanted and loose due to the pressure, and the frame was damaged.\n\nWe submitted an online request, which was closed with the explanation that a box spring was required (something we were never told). We were advised to return to the store and deal with them (we live in Ndip and the store is in Vaudreuil, therefore not a short drive and making this now our second visit there), however Mike wasn't there that day and we were advised to go back home and he would give us a call.\n\nA few days later, Mike called and asked us to come in again to discuss the situation in person (third visit).\n\nMike was extremely understanding and genuinely tried to help. We attempted to exchange the frame, but the alternative one we wanted wasn’t available in king size.\n\nHe then offered replacement parts, but the frame itself was damaged, which we clearly showed in photos.\n\nMike escalated the issue to the store manager.\n\nThe manager offered two options:\n\n1.\tBuy a box spring and they would give us a new bed frame\n2.\tReceive store credit\n\nWe chose the store credit, but were then told we had to bring the broken bed frame back ourselves, even though it was damaged and they planned to discard it. We explained that we drive small cars (a Fiat 500) but this was dismissed.\n\nDuring all of this, we were sleeping with our new mattress on the floor. (since the frame is broken)\n\nWe eventually managed to transport the broken frame back (our fourth visit) and received the store credit.\n\nWe then purchased a proper bed frame from The Brick.\n\nNow on our fifth visit to the store, we tried to use the store credit to buy a sound bar. We were told that delivery would cost $60 because the purchase was under $500.\n\nGiven everything we had gone through over the last three weeks and five visits in, we asked if the fee could be waived. Patrick responded immediately with a rude and dismissive “no.”\n\nWe now have to return a sixth time just to pick up the sound bar.\n\nWhile Mike was absolutely wonderful, patient, kind, and professional, it’s the overall operation and management who were extremely disappointing.\n\nSave yourself time, money, and stress and go to a proper furniture store.",
        "time": 1767876395,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Sigfredo Giron",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/102594939421148751746/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a/ACg8ocJ31lBj7YSUXZ8dpKWa53Y26hYxuItokAn6HbzHhx8cdWdnyw=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
        "rating": 1,
        "relative_time_description": "a month ago",
        "text": "We were misinformed, sent back and forth for weeks with five store visits, forced to transport a broken bed frame ourselves, and ultimately met with dismissive management—save yourself the time and shop elsewhere.\nStuck paying 400$ for a broken bedframe\nHad to buy another one at a different store",
        "time": 1767137327,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "Lisa LeBlanc",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/103926530976221004337/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjUIhIGOmmkN-ngaUb31zLPZmQneM66l6RcJ5zrZEeivhdXlzGwF=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo-ba3",
        "rating": 5,
        "relative_time_description": "a year ago",
        "text": "I am very pleased with the service. Thank you, Melanie! It was relaxed, no pushy sales, but informative and helpful.\n\nThe delivery guys arrived early during the alloted time frame  and had to bring my beautiful new couch up two flights of stairs. They did so very efficiently.\n\nI was advised at the store that some assembly would be required and which tools to have on-hand, so all went smoothly.\n\nThe couch is extremely well built, sturdy, firm, and so comfy! I absolutely love it! It also has a very good warranty, and is made in Canada.\n\nOnly one tiny negative blip, the outer plastic packaging was amazingly dirty! Thankfully, though, the couch was well protected and clean inside.\n\nLast and not least, this was a great deal compared to other stores. At those stores I was resigned to buying a couch without a cuddler because there was at least a $300 difference. So glad I went to RD because for only $100 (instead of $300) more at RD, I got what I really wanted.\n\nVery satisfied customer! I highly recommend RD Furniture in Vaudreuil and wish them all the best.",
        "time": 1730568344,
        "translated": false
      },
      {
        "author_name": "sabribri :3",
        "author_url": "https://www.google.com/maps/contrib/111431637548611879592/reviews",
        "language": "en",
        "original_language": "en",
        "profile_photo_url": "https://lh3.googleusercontent.com/a-/ALV-UjWQ59kyMvonnRCiQnCWobnckhLrdzfuDs8hiXuMsyj4ole0Sw8=s128-c0x00000000-cc-rp-mo",
